    "en": "Yu",
    "zh": "余",
    "history": "The Yu surname traces back to ancient China through two primary accounts. One credits Youyu, an official under Duke Mu of Qin during the Spring and Autumn period (770-476 BC), who helped establish Qin as a regional power and pioneered concepts of benevolent governance. An alternative account links the surname to descendants of Yu the Great, the legendary ancient emperor, specifically through his youngest son Sihan, who was appointed King of the Yu territory.",
    "historyZh": "余姓的起源主要有两种说法,均可追溯至中国古代。一种说法认为该姓源自由余,春秋时期(公元前770年至前476年)秦穆公属下的官员,他协助秦国确立了地区强国的地位,并开创了仁政的理念。另一种说法则将该姓与传说中的上古帝王大禹的后代联系起来,具体为其幼子思汉,被封为余地之王。",
    "famous": "Eu Tong Sen (1877-1936) - Self-made Hokkien millionaire from Penang who built his fortune through mining, rubber, and real estate, and founded the Eu Yan Sang traditional Chinese medicine brand; Eu Tong Sen Street in Singapore was named in his honour in 1919.",
    "famousZh": "余东旋（1877-1936）- 出身槟城的白手起家福建籍富商，凭借矿业、橡胶业及地产业积累财富，创立余仁生中药品牌；新加坡余东旋街于1919年以他命名，以示纪念。",
