    "history": "The surname Hou can trace its origins to Marquis Min of Jin (晋侯缗), who lived during the Spring and Autumn period (771-476 BC). Marquis Min was overthrown by his relative, who would become the new Duke Wu of Jin. Marquis Min’s descendants escaped from the state of Jin, and adopted Hou (侯) as their surname, which means “marquis” in Chinese.",
