    "en": "Guan",
    "zh": "关",
    "history": "There are two main sources for the Guan surname. According to one account, the Guans are descended of a Grand Minister called Guan Fenglong, who lived during the Xia Dynasty. The family settled in modern-day Shanxi Province, and later prospered in Gansu Province.\n\nAccording to another account, the surname is derived of an official post called the \"Guanling\" or the \"Director of the Pass\". Guanling was the official guard at strategic points along the borders, responsible for protecting the realm against foreign intruders. The surname Guan was later adopted by any descendants of those who held this post. These descendants primarily settled in Shandong and Jiangsu provinces. \n\nThe surname is popular today among ethnic minorities such as the Zhuang people and the Mongols.",
    "historyZh": "关姓主要有两个来源。一种说法认为,关氏源自夏朝一位名为关龙逄的大臣。该家族最初定居于今山西省,后来在甘肃省繁衍兴盛。\n\n另一种说法则认为,此姓源自一个名为“关令”(即“关隘长官”)的官职。关令是驻守边境要隘的官员,负责抵御外敌、保卫疆土。后来,凡曾任此职者的后代便以“关”为姓。这些后代主要定居于山东、江苏两省。\n\n如今,此姓在壮族、蒙古族等少数民族中亦颇为常见。",
