    "en": "Shi",
    "zh": "史",
    "history": "The surname Shi can trace its roots back to Yin Yi (尹佚), a court historian at the start of the Zhou Dynasty (1046 - 256 BC). He was well-respected for his sense of righteousness and responsibility as a historian. Some of Yin Yi’s descendants would eventually come to adopt Shi (史) as their surname, in honour of their ancestor’s role as a court historian, or taishi (太史) in Chinese.",
    "historyZh": "史姓可追溯至周朝(公元前1046年至前256年)初年的宫廷史官尹佚。他因秉持正义、恪尽史官职责而备受敬重。尹佚的部分后代为纪念先祖担任太史一职,便以“史”为姓。",
