    "en": "Lyu",
    "zh": "吕",
    "history": "From the name of the ancient state of Lü, in present-day Henan province. Boyi (伯夷), a descendant of the Yan Emperor, had assisted Yu the Great in controlling the legendary great floods that plagued China for at least two generations. In recognition of Boyi’s contributions, Yu the Great granted him the state of Lü. During the Spring and Autumn period (771 - 476 BC), the State of Lü was conquered by the State of Chu, after which Boyi’s descendants adopted Lü as their surname.",
    "historyZh": "源自古吕国之名,位于今河南省境内。炎帝后裔伯夷曾协助大禹治理困扰中国至少两代人的滔天洪水。大禹为表彰伯夷的功绩,将吕地封给他。春秋时期(公元前771年至前476年),吕国被楚国所灭,伯夷的后代遂以吕为姓。",
