    "history": "The Wu surname originated from the ancient state of Wu in present-day Jiangsu province. During the 13th century BC, two sons of King Tai of Zhou, Taibo and Zhongyang, relocated southeast and established this powerful state, and their descendants subsequently adopted Wu as their surname. One of the most celebrated rulers of Wu was King Helu, regarded as one of the \"Five Hegemons of China\" during the Spring and Autumn period, cementing the clan's historical prominence.",
    "historyZh": "吴姓起源于位于今江苏省境内的古吴国。公元前13世纪,周太王的两个儿子太伯与仲雍南迁至此,建立了这一强盛的国家,其后代遂以吴为姓。吴国最负盛名的君主之一是吴王阖闾,被誉为春秋时期“五霸”之一,进一步奠定了吴氏家族的历史声望。",
