    "en": "Tang",
    "zh": "唐",
    "history": "From a place called Tang, in present-day Shanxi province. The legendary Yellow Emperor (2697–2595 BC) granted this region to his son Dan Zhu, whose descendants eventually adopted it as their surname. They held power in the region until they were conquered by Cheng Wang, second king (1115–1079 BC) of the Zhou dynasty. Cheng Wang granted the region to his brother Shu Yu, whose descendants also adopted the place name Tang as a surname. This character was later used for the Tang dynasty, which lasted between 618 and 907 AD.",
    "historyZh": "源自位于今山西省境内的一处名为“唐”的地方。传说中的黄帝(公元前2697年至前2595年)将此地封给其子丹朱,其后代最终以此为姓。他们在此地统治,直至被周朝第二代君主成王(公元前1115年至前1079年)所灭。成王将此地封给其弟叔虞,叔虞的后代也以地名“唐”为姓。此字后来也被用作唐朝(公元618年至907年)的国号。",
