    "en": "Xia",
    "zh": "夏",
    "history": "The surname Xia can trace its roots to the Yu the Great, an ancient Chinese king who founded the Xia dynasty, traditionally considered the first dynasty in Chinese history. It is said that Yu the Great was famed for subduing the legendary floods plaguing China, through his diligence and engineering work. Emperor Shun, who was the reigning emperor then, was so impressed by Yu’s abilities that he passed the throne to Yu instead of his own son, thus beginning the Xia dynasty. After the Xia dynasty was conquered by the Shang dynasty, following the defeat of its tyrannical last king Jie, some of the Xia dynasty’s descendants adopted Xia as their surname.",
    "historyZh": "夏姓可追溯至大禹,中国古代一位建立了夏朝的君王,夏朝被传统上视为中国历史上第一个朝代。相传大禹因治理中国的滔天洪水而声名远扬,他勤勉不懈,工程卓著。当时在位的帝舜对大禹的才能十分赞赏,遂将王位禅让给大禹,而非传给自己的儿子,夏朝由此开启。夏朝末代暴君桀战败后,夏朝被商朝所灭,部分夏朝后裔便以夏为姓。",
