    "en": "Yao",
    "zh": "姚",
    "history": "The surname Yao is one of the oldest-known surnames in China. The left-half of the word Yao is the word “女”, or “woman”, suggesting that the surname may have existed when China was still a matrilineal society. Legend says that Emperor Shun was born in a place called Yaoxu (姚墟) in present-day Henan province, and adopted Yao as his surname. Many of Emperor Shun’s descendants would later adopt their own surnames, but some retained Yao as their surname till this day.",
    "historyZh": "姚姓是中国已知最古老的姓氏之一。“姚”字左半边为“女”字,暗示该姓氏或许起源于中国仍处于母系社会之时。相传帝舜出生于今河南省境内一处名为姚墟的地方,遂以姚为姓。帝舜的许多后代后来各自采用了不同的姓氏,但部分后裔仍沿用姚姓,传承至今。",
