    "en": "Jiang",
    "zh": "姜",
    "history": "The surname Jiang is one of the oldest-known surnames in China. The bottom-half of the word Jiang is the word “女”, or “woman”, suggesting that the surname may have existed when China was still a matrilineal society. Legend says that the Yan Emperor was born at the Jiang River (姜水), and would adopt Jiang as his surname. Although many of Yan Emperor’s descendants would later adopt other surnames, some of them retained Jiang as their surname, which has survived till this day.",
    "historyZh": "姜姓是中国已知最古老的姓氏之一。“姜”字下半部为“女”字,暗示该姓氏或许起源于中国仍处于母系社会之时。相传炎帝出生于姜水岸边,遂以姜为姓。尽管炎帝的许多后代后来改用其他姓氏,但其中一部分仍沿用姜姓,并一直传承至今。",
