    "en": "Cui",
    "zh": "崔",
    "history": "The surname Cui can trace its roots back to Ji Zi (季子), a nobleman from the state of Qi. When Duke Ding of Qi died in 975 BC, Ji Zi, as his eldest son, should have inherited the Qi throne. Instead, he gave up his claim and let his younger brother become the new duke, Duke Yi of Qi. Ji Zi had a fief at the region of Cui, located in present-day Shandong province, and his descendants later came to adopt Cui as their surname.",
    "historyZh": "崔姓可追溯至齐国贵族季子。公元前975年齐丁公去世时,身为长子的季子本应继承齐国君位,但他放弃了继承权,让弟弟即位,是为齐乙公。季子在今山东省境内的崔地拥有封邑,其后代后来便以崔为姓。",
