    "en": "Chang",
    "zh": "常",
    "history": "The surname Chang has multiple origins. During the reign of the Yellow Emperor, there was Chang Yi (常仪) who was in charge of lunar divination, and Chang Xian (常先) who was an official in charge of public works. Their descendants are said to have adopted Chang as their surname. Interestingly, Chang Yi is believed to have inspired the story of Chang’e, the Chinese goddess of the Moon. Another origin story traces the surname Chang back to Wei Kang Shu (卫康叔), younger brother of King Wu of Zhou. A descendant of Wei Kang Shu was granted the region of Chang (常), and thus his descendants adopted Chang as their surname as well.",
    "historyZh": "常姓有多种起源。黄帝在位期间,有负责月相占卜的常仪,以及负责公共工程的官员常先,相传他们的后代便以常为姓。有趣的是,常仪据信正是嫦娥传说的灵感来源,嫦娥是中国神话中的月神。另一起源说法则追溯至周武王之弟卫康叔。卫康叔的一位后代受封于常地,其后代因此也以常为姓。",
