    "en": "Zhang",
    "zh": "张",
    "history": "According to legend, the Zhang surname originated with Zhang Hui, grandson of the Yellow Emperor, who was honoured for his expertise in weapon production, particularly bows and arrows - the character 张 itself combines the characters for \"bow\" and \"long.\" His descendants settled in Qingyang, in modern-day Qinghe county, Hubei, establishing the clan's ancestral homeland. Zhang is the 18th most common surname in China and has spread worldwide through successive waves of migration.",
    "historyZh": "相传张姓起源于黄帝之孙张挥,他因精于兵器制造、尤擅弓箭而备受尊崇——“张”字本身正是由“弓”与“长”二字组合而成。他的后代定居于今湖北省清河县一带的青阳,奠定了该家族的祖居之地。张姓是中国第18大姓,历经数代迁徙已遍布世界各地。",
    "famous": "Chang Yun Chung - Singaporean billionaire and shipping tycoon who founded Pacific International Lines, once recognised as the world's oldest billionaire.",
