    "en": "Peng",
    "zh": "彭",
    "history": "The surname Peng can trace its roots back to Peng Zu (彭祖). A descendant of Emperor Zhuanxu, Peng Zu was skilled at making wild chicken soup, which earned him the recognition of Emperor Yao. As such, Emperor Yao granted the state of Peng (彭) in present-day Jiangsu province to Peng Zu. Interestingly, legend says that Peng Zu lived up to a ripe old age of 800, and was deified upon his passing. His descendants eventually came to adopt Peng as their surname.",
    "historyZh": "彭姓可追溯至彭祖。彭祖是颛顼帝的后裔,擅长烹制野鸡汤,因此获得帝尧的赏识。帝尧遂将位于今江苏省境内的彭地封给彭祖。有趣的是,相传彭祖享年八百岁高寿,去世后被尊奉为神。他的后代后来便以彭为姓。",
