    "en": "Xu",
    "zh": "徐",
    "history": "The Xu surname traces back to Boyi, a legendary tribal leader of the 2nd millennium BC credited with helping to control the Great Flood. After the state of Xu was conquered by the state of Wu in 512 BC, its descendants adopted Xu as their family name in commemoration of their fallen nation. An alternative origin links the surname to the Rebellion of the Three Guards (1042-1039 BC), when the Duke of Zhou divided Shang dynasty loyalist factions into six clans, one of which bore the Xu name.",
    "historyZh": "徐姓可追溯至伯益,公元前2千纪一位传说中的部落首领,曾协助治理滔天洪水。公元前512年徐国被吴国所灭后,其后代为纪念故国,便以徐为姓。另一种说法则将该姓与“三监之乱”(公元前1042年至前1039年)联系起来,当时周公将忠于商朝的遗民势力分为六族,其中一族即以徐为姓。",
