    "en": "Dai",
    "zh": "戴",
    "history": "The surname Dai has two origins. The first originates from the ancient state of Dai located in present-day Henan province, said to be descended from Shang nobility. After the state of Dai was conquered by the state of Zheng during the Spring and Autumn period (771 - 476 BC), its descendants adopted Dai as their surname. The second origin story states that the surname originates from the posthumous name of Duke Dai of Song, whose descendants later adopted Dai as their surname as well.",
    "historyZh": "戴姓有两个起源。第一个源自位于今河南省境内的古戴国,相传其先祖为商朝贵族。春秋时期(公元前771年至前476年)戴国被郑国所灭后,其后代便以戴为姓。第二个起源说法则认为,此姓源自宋戴公的谥号,其后代后来也以戴为姓。",
