    "zh": "文",
    "history": "The surname Wen has multiple origins. One origin traces its roots to King Wen of Zhou, who was posthumously honoured as the founder of the Zhou dynasty (1046-256 BC). Some of his descendants were said to have adopted Wen as their surname. Another origin story states that the surname Wen came from the founder of the ancient state of Xu, Xu Wen Shu (许文叔). Some of his descendants also came to adopt Wen as their surname.",
    "historyZh": "文姓有多种起源。其一可追溯至周文王,他被后世尊奉为周朝(公元前1046年至前256年)的奠基者。相传他的部分后代便以文为姓。另一种说法则认为,文姓源自古许国的开国君主许文叔。他的部分后代后来也以文为姓。",
