    "en": "Fang",
    "zh": "方",
    "history": "The surname Fang has two origins. The first originates from Lei (雷), a descendant of the Yan Emperor. Lei fought alongside the Yellow Emperor against Chiyou (蚩尤), and as such was rewarded with the region of Fangshan (方山) in present-day Henan province. Some of his descendants would adopt Fang as their surname. The second origin can trace its roots to Fang Shu (方叔), who was an official during the reign of King Xuan of Zhou (828 BC - 782 BC). Fang Shu was rewarded with the region of Luo (洛) after fighting a victorious battle against the state of Chu, and his descendants would adopt his name, Fang, as their surname.",
    "historyZh": "方姓有两个起源。第一个源自炎帝后裔雷。雷曾协助黄帝与蚩尤交战,因此受封于今河南省境内的方山地区。他的部分后代便以方为姓。第二个起源可追溯至方叔,周宣王(公元前828年至前782年)在位期间的一位官员。方叔因在对楚战役中获胜而受封于洛地,其后代便以他的名字“方”为姓。",
