    "en": "Yi",
    "zh": "易",
    "history": "The surname Yi has two different origins. The first origin traces its roots to the ancient state of Zhongshan, located in present-day Hebei province. When it was eventually conquered by the much more powerful state of Zhao in 296 BC, King Shang of Zhongshan and his people were relocated to present-day Shanxi province, and adopted Yi as their surname. The second origin traces its roots to Jiang Ziya (姜子牙), a military advisor at the start of the Zhou Dynasty (1046 - 256 BC) who would later found the powerful state of Qi. One of his descendants was granted the land of Yi, located in present-day Hebei province. This branch would eventually adopt Yi as their surname as well.",
    "historyZh": "易姓有两种不同的起源。第一个可追溯至位于今河北省境内的古中山国。公元前296年,中山国被更为强大的赵国所灭后,中山王尚及其子民被迁往今山西省境内,并以易为姓。第二个起源可追溯至姜子牙,周朝(公元前1046年至前256年)初年的一位军事谋士,他后来建立了强盛的齐国。他的一位后代受封于位于今河北省境内的易地。这一支系最终也以易为姓。",
