    "en": "Zhu",
    "zh": "朱",
    "history": "From the name of the ancient state of Zhu 邾, located in present-day Shandong province. At the start of the Zhou Dynasty (1046 - 256 BC), Cao Jia, a descendant of the legendary emperor Zhuanxu, was bestowed lordship of the state of Zhu. Later, this state was conquered by the state of Chu. Cao Jia's descendants fled their state, and from that moment on, dropped the part of the surname meaning \"country\" (阝), indicating that they had been separated from their ancestral home.",
