    "en": "Li",
    "zh": "李",
    "history": "The surname Li evolved from the ancient Ying lineage, descending from Emperor Zhuanxu. Tradition holds that General Gaoyao's descendants first adopted the character 理 (meaning \"reason\") as their surname. This later changed to 李 (\"plum\") through a legendary tale: Li Zheng, a minister who opposed the cruel Shang King Zhou, was executed, and his son Li Lizhen survived in hiding by eating wild plums, afterwards changing the family name to Li in gratitude. Li is today one of the most common surnames in China.",
    "historyZh": "李姓源自古代嬴姓一脉,为颛顼帝的后裔。相传大将皋陶的后代最初以“理”(意为“道理”“司法”)为姓。后来因一则传说而改为“李”(意为“李子”):大臣理征因反对暴虐的商纣王而被处死,其子理利贞为躲避追捕而隐姓埋名,靠食用野生李子存活,后为感念李子的救命之恩而改姓“李”。李姓如今是中国最常见的姓氏之一。",
    "famous": "Lee Kuan Yew - Singapore's founding Prime Minister, regarded as the \"founding father of Singapore\" and one of the most prominent bearers of the Li surname in modern history.",
    "famousZh": "李光耀（Lee Kuan Yew）- 新加坡建国总理，被誉为“新加坡国父”，是现代史上李姓最具代表性的人物之一。",
