    "en": "Liang",
    "zh": "梁",
    "history": "From the name of Liang Mountain in present-day Shaanxi province. During the reign of Zhou dynasty emperor Xuan Wang (827–782 BC), Qin Zhong set out on an expedition to subdue the barbarians to the west, in Central Asia. Qin Zhong was killed, and his five sons set out to avenge their father, eventually succeeding and defeating the peoples of the west. The emperor divided the area of Shang among them, and the second son received the area around Liang Mountain. His descendants thereafter adopted the surname Liang. In later times, Liang was the name of two Chinese dynasties, the Southern Liang Dynasty (502–557) and the Western Liang Dynasty (907–923).",
    "historyZh": "源自位于今陕西省境内的梁山之名。周宣王(公元前827年至前782年)在位期间,秦仲奉命出征,讨伐西部中亚一带的游牧部族。秦仲在战中遇害,其五子誓师为父报仇,最终成功击败西戎。周王将商地分封给五子,次子受封于梁山一带。其后代此后便以梁为姓。后世,梁还曾是中国两个朝代的国号,即南梁(公元502年至557年)与西梁(公元907年至923年)。",
