    "en": "Wu",
    "zh": "武",
    "history": "The surname Wu has multiple origins. One origin story traces its roots back to King Ping of Zhou. When King Ping’s youngest son was born, it was said that the lines on his palm resembled the ancient character for the word Wu, and so this son’s descendants adopted Wu as their surname. Other origins suggest the surname came from King Wu Ding during the Shang Dynasty, or Duke Wu of Song during the Spring and Autumn period (771-476 BC).",
    "historyZh": "武姓有多种起源。一种说法追溯至周平王。相传周平王幼子出生时,其掌纹形似古代“武”字,因此这一支后代便以武为姓。另有说法认为,此姓源自商朝的武丁王,或春秋时期(公元前771年至前476年)的宋武公。",
