    "en": "Duan",
    "zh": "段",
    "history": "The surname Duan can trace its roots to Gong Shu Duan (共叔段), the younger brother of Duke Zhuang of Zheng during the Spring and Autumn period (771-476 BC). Gong Shu Duan attempted to usurp the throne from Duke Zhuang but failed, and escaped to the region of Gong (located in present-day Henan province). When Duke Zhuang’s son Duke Li inherited the throne, he invited Gong Shu Duan’s descendants back to the sate of Zheng. These descendants would eventually adopt Duan as their surname.",
    "historyZh": "段姓可追溯至共叔段,春秋时期(公元前771年至前476年)郑庄公之弟。共叔段曾图谋篡夺庄公之位,事败后逃往今河南省境内的共地。郑庄公之子郑厉公继位后,邀请共叔段的后代重返郑国。这些后代最终便以段为姓。",
