    "history": "From the name of the ancient state of Mao, located in present-day Henan province. At the start of the Zhou Dynasty (1046 - 256 BC), Mao Shu Zheng (毛叔郑), younger brother of King Wu of Zhou, was granted the state of Mao. When the state of Mao was eventually conquered by the state of Qin during the Spring and Autumn period (771-476 BC), its descendants adopted Mao as their surname.",
