    "en": "Jiang",
    "zh": "江",
    "history": "From the name of the ancient state of Jiang, located in present-day Henan province. Boyi (伯益), a descendant of Emperor Zhuanxu, was granted the state of Jiang at the start of the Zhou Dynasty (1046 - 256 BC). However, being surrounded by powerful states like Chu, Song, and Qi, as well as constant floods from the Huai River, the state of Jiang did not last long. Eventually, it was conquered by the state of Chu, and its descendants adopted Jiang as their surname.",
    "historyZh": "源自位于今河南省境内的古江国之名。颛顼帝的后裔伯益,在周朝(公元前1046年至前256年)初年受封于江国。然而,由于四周环绕着楚、宋、齐等强国,加之淮河水患不断,江国并未长久存续。最终,江国被楚国所灭,其后代便以江为姓。",
