    "history": "The surname Wang is said to have two different origins. The first originates from the ancient state of Wangmang (汪芒), located in present-day Zhejiang province. When the state of Wangmang was conquered by the state of Chu, its descendants settled in present-day Anhui province and adopted Wang, a shortened version of Wangmang, as their surname. The second origin story says that Duke Cheng of Lu granted the region of Yingchuan (颍川) to his second son Wang (汪), and his descendants would come to adopt Wang as their surname.",
    "historyZh": "汪姓相传有两个不同的起源。第一个源自位于今浙江省境内的古汪芒国。汪芒国被楚国所灭后,其后代迁居今安徽省境内,并以“汪芒”的简称“汪”为姓。另一种说法则称,鲁成公将颍川地区封给次子汪,其后代便以汪为姓。",
