    "en": "Xiong",
    "zh": "熊",
    "history": "The surname Xiong can trace its roots back to Yu Xiong (鬻熊), an official during the reign of King Wen of Zhou (1125-1051 BC). Yu Xiong was a descendant of Emperor Zhuanxu, and said to have been a teacher of King Wen himself. Yu Xiong’s great-grandson, Xiong Yi (熊绎), would later found the powerful state of Chu. When the state of Chu was eventually conquered by the state of Qin during the end of the Warring States period (475-221 BC), some of its descendants adopted Xiong as their surname, in honour of their ancestor Yu Xiong.",
    "historyZh": "熊姓可追溯至鬻熊,周文王(公元前1125年至前1051年)在位期间的一位官员。鬻熊是颛顼帝的后裔,相传还曾是周文王的老师。鬻熊的曾孙熊绎后来建立了强盛的楚国。战国末期(公元前475年至前221年)楚国被秦国所灭后,其部分后代为纪念先祖鬻熊,便以熊为姓。",
