    "en": "Tian",
    "zh": "田",
    "history": "The surname Tian can trace its roots to Chen Wan (陈完), also known as Tian Wan (田完). Chen Wan was originally a prince from the state of Chen, who later escaped to the state of Qi to avoid conflict. Duke Huan of Qi, who reigned from 685 to 643 BC, recognised Chen Wan’s abilities and made him an official. As the ancient pronunciations of Chen (陈) and Tian (田) were similar, Chen Wan was also known as Tian Wan, and his descendants would come to adopt Tian as their surname.",
    "historyZh": "田姓可追溯至陈完,又称田完。陈完原是陈国王子,后为避祸逃往齐国。齐桓公(在位期间为公元前685年至前643年)赏识陈完的才能,任命他为官。由于“陈”与“田”二字古音相近,陈完也被称为田完,其后代后来便以田为姓。",
