    "en": "Bai",
    "zh": "白",
    "history": "The surname Bai has multiple origin stories. One of them traces its roots back to Bai Fu (白阜), an official during the Yan Emperor’s time who was known for his efforts in dredging waterways. His descendants are said to have adopted Bai as their surname. Another story states that during the Spring and Autumn period (771-476 BC), a nobleman from the state of Chu named Bai Gong Sheng (白公胜) attempted to seize the throne from his cousin, Duke Hui of Chu. When he failed, Bai Gong Sheng committed suicide. As he had earlier been granted the region of Baidi (白地), located in present-day Henan province, his descendants adopted Bai as their surname. Notably, Bai is also a major surname among Chinese Muslims, most of whom descend from ancient Central Asian travellers.",
    "historyZh": "白姓有多种起源说法。其一可追溯至白阜,炎帝时期的一位官员,以疏浚河道的功绩著称。相传他的后代便以白为姓。另一说法称,春秋时期(公元前771年至前476年),楚国贵族白公胜图谋从堂兄楚惠王手中夺取王位。事败后,白公胜自尽身亡。由于他此前曾受封于今河南省境内的白地,其后代便以白为姓。值得一提的是,白姓也是中国穆斯林中的主要姓氏之一,其中大多数人的祖先为古代中亚旅行者。",
