    "zh": "盛",
    "history": "The surname Sheng can trace its origins to Shao Gong Shi (召公奭), a high-ranking minister at the start of the Zhou Dynasty (1046-256 BC). He was granted the state of Yan as a reward for helping King Wu of Zhou overthrow the Shang Dynasty. Some of his descendants adopted his name, Shi (奭), as their surname. During the Han Dynasty, in order to avoid the naming taboo of Emperor Yuan of Han (75-33 BC), whose personal name was Liu Shi (刘奭), Shao Gong Shi’s descendants changed their surname from Shi to Sheng.",
    "historyZh": "盛姓可追溯至召公奭,周朝(公元前1046年至前256年)初年的一位高级大臣。他因协助周武王推翻商朝有功,受封于燕国。他的部分后代以其名“奭”为姓。汉代时,为避汉元帝(公元前75年至前33年)刘奭名讳,召公奭的后代便将姓氏由“奭”改为“盛”。",
