    "en": "Cheng",
    "zh": "程",
    "history": "From the name of the ancient state of Cheng, located in present-day Henan province. At the start of the Zhou Dynasty (1046 - 256 BC), Bofu (伯符) was granted the state of Cheng, in reward for fighting alongside the Zhou kings. Bofu could trace his roots back to Emperor Zhuanxu, who was in turn the Yellow Emperor’s grandson. When the state of Cheng fell during the Spring and Autumn period (771-476 BC), its descendants adopted Cheng as their surname.",
    "historyZh": "源自位于今河南省境内的古程国之名。周朝(公元前1046年至前256年)初年,伯符因随周王征战有功而受封于程国。伯符的世系可追溯至颛顼帝,而颛顼帝则是黄帝之孙。春秋时期(公元前771年至前476年)程国灭亡后,其后代便以程为姓。",
