    "en": "Zhang",
    "zh": "章",
    "history": "From the name of the ancient state of Zhang (鄣), located in present-day Shandong province. At the start of the Zhou Dynasty (1046-256 BC), the state of Zhang became a vassal state under the state of Qi, ruled by Jiang Ziya (姜子牙). Jiang Ziya then granted the state of Zhang to one of his sons. Eventually, the state of Zhang was conquered by the state of Qi, and its descendants took on the surname Zhang (章), dropping the part meaning “country” (阝).",
    "historyZh": "源自位于今山东省境内的古鄣国之名。周朝(公元前1046年至前256年)初年,鄣国成为齐国的附庸,齐国由姜子牙统治。姜子牙随后将鄣国封给其一子。鄣国最终被齐国所灭,其后代遂以“章”为姓,去掉姓氏中表示“国”的偏旁“阝”。",
