    "en": "Luo",
    "zh": "罗",
    "history": "From the name of the state of Luo, in existence during the Zhou dynasty (1046–256 BC). The state of Luo was granted to a mythical figure called Zhurong, who in folk religion is considered the god of fire and of the south. He is also believed to be descended of the Yellow Emperor. Subsequently, his descendants adopted the state name as their surname.\n\nAccording to another legend, the Luos are the descendants of an ancient tribe who were responsible for knitting nets for the capture of birds: the character \"luo\" means \"capturing with net\".",
    "historyZh": "源自周朝(公元前1046年至前256年)时期存在的罗国之名。罗国封给了传说人物祝融,民间信仰中他被奉为火神与南方之神,相传也是黄帝的后裔。此后,他的后代便以国名为姓。\n\n另有传说称,罗氏是古代一支负责编织捕鸟之网的部落的后裔:“罗”字本义即为“以网捕捉”。",
