    "en": "Su",
    "zh": "苏",
    "history": "From the name of the ancient state of Su (苏), in present-day Henan province. During the Xia Dynasty, King Huai of Xia granted the region of Yousu (有苏) to Emperor Zhuanxu’s descendant Kunwu (昆吾), which eventually became the state of Su. When the state of Su fell during the Shang Dynasty, its descendants adopted Su as their surname. One of them, Su Fensheng (苏忿生), would later become Minister of Justice (司寇) to King Wu of Zhou, and be granted the state of Wen (温).",
    "historyZh": "源自位于今河南省境内的古苏国之名。夏朝时,夏怀王将有苏之地封给颛顼帝的后裔昆吾,该地后来发展为苏国。商朝时苏国灭亡后,其后代便以苏为姓。其中一位后裔苏忿生,后来成为周武王麾下的司寇,受封于温国。",
