    "en": "Fan",
    "zh": "范",
    "history": "The surname Fan can trace its roots back to Emperor Yao. One of his descendants, Shi Hui (士会), was a military commander under the state of Jin, during the Spring and Autumn period (771-476 BC). In recognition of his achievements, Shi Hui was granted the region of Fan in present-day Henan province, and would be known posthumously as Fan Wuzi (范武子). His descendants would adopt Fan as their surname as well.",
    "historyZh": "范姓可追溯至帝尧。他的一位后裔士会,是春秋时期(公元前771年至前476年)晋国的一位军事统帅。因战功卓著,士会受封于今河南省境内的范地,死后被尊称为范武子。他的后代后来也以范为姓。",
