    "en": "Xiao",
    "zh": "萧",
    "history": "From the name of the ancient state of Xiao (located in present-day Anhui province), a vassal state of the state of Song. The state of Xiao was granted to a Song nobleman named Xiao Shu Daxin (萧叔大心), who had helped Duke Huan of Song regain power over the state of Song from the rebellious Nangong Changwan (南宫长万). After the state of Xiao was conquered by the state of Chu in 597 BC, Xiao Shu Daxin’s descendants adopted Xiao as their surname.",
    "historyZh": "源自古萧国之名(位于今安徽省境内),为宋国的附庸国。萧国封给了宋国贵族萧叔大心,他曾协助宋桓公从作乱的南宫长万手中夺回宋国政权。公元前597年萧国被楚国所灭后,萧叔大心的后代便以萧为姓。",
