    "en": "Dong",
    "zh": "董",
    "history": "The surname Dong can trace its roots back to the legendary Emperor Zhuanxu. It is said that Dong Fu (董父), a descendant of Emperor Zhuanxu, was skilled in the taming of dragons. Emperor Shun, the emperor at the time, appointed Dong Fu with the job of raising and training dragons. Dong Fu managed to teach the dragons various dances, greatly pleasing Emperor Shun who then granted Dong Fu the land of Zongchuan (鬷川) in present-day Shanxi province, as well as the surname Dong. Today, his descendants still bear the surname of Dong.",
    "historyZh": "董姓可追溯至传说中的颛顼帝。相传颛顼帝的后裔董父擅长驯龙。当时在位的帝舜委任董父负责饲养、训练神龙。董父成功教会神龙表演各种舞蹈,深得帝舜赏识,帝舜遂将今山西省境内的鬷川之地连同董姓一并赐给董父。如今,他的后代仍沿用董姓。",
