    "history": "From the name of the ancient state of Xue, located in present-day Shandong province. Xi Zhong (奚仲), a descendant of the Yellow Emperor, was said to have invented the ancient Chinese chariot during the reign of Yu the Great. In recognition of his work, Yu the Great granted Xi Zhong the state of Xue. Xi Zhong’s descendants would later adopt Xue as their surname.",
