    "en": "Yuan",
    "zh": "袁",
    "history": "The surname Yuan can trace its roots back to Yuan Taotu (辕涛图), a 7th-century BC nobleman from the state of Chen. Yuan Taotu was granted the land of Yangxia (阳夏) in present-day Henan province, and took the second character in his grandfather’s style name, Boyuan (伯爰), as his own family name. Initially, the surname was written in numerous ways, including “袁”, “辕”, and “爰” (all pronounced Yuan), until the Qin Dynasty (221 - 206 BC) when “袁” emerged as the standardised form still in use today.",
    "historyZh": "袁姓可追溯至辕涛涂,公元前7世纪陈国的一位贵族。辕涛涂受封于今河南省境内的阳夏之地,并取其祖父表字“伯爰”中的第二字作为自己的姓氏。最初,此姓曾以多种字形书写,包括“袁”“辕”“爰”(均读作yuán),直至秦朝(公元前221年至前206年)“袁”字才成为沿用至今的标准写法。",
