    "history": "From an area called Xie, in present-day Nanyang of Henan province. Xuan Wang, the penultimate king (827–781 BC) of the Western Zhou dynasty, granted this area to one of his brothers-in-law. The people of Xie later adopted the name of the state as their surname.\n\nIn the Eastern Jin dynasty (317 - 120 AD), the Xie were among the cluster of noble clans who fled to the south in the wake of the fall of the capital of Chang'an, dominating the court thereafter.",
    "historyZh": "源自位于今河南省南阳的一处名为“谢”的地方。西周倒数第二位君主周宣王(公元前827年至前781年)将此地封给其一位姻亲。谢地的人民后来便以国名为姓。\n\n东晋时期(公元317年至420年),谢氏是随都城长安陷落而南迁的一批世家大族之一,此后长期把持朝政。",
