    "en": "He",
    "zh": "贺",
    "history": "The surname He can trace its roots to Duke Huan of Qi. One of his great-grandsons, Qing Feng (庆封), adopted Qing as his surname, in honour of his father Gongsun Qingke (公孙庆克). However, during the reign of Emperor An of Han (106-125), Qing Feng's descendants were forced to change their surname as it broke the naming taboo of Emperor An's father, Liu Qing (刘庆). Thus, they changed their surname from Qing (庆) to He (贺), both meaning \"to celebrate\".",
    "historyZh": "贺姓可追溯至齐桓公。他的一位曾孙庆封,为纪念父亲公孙庆克而以“庆”为姓。然而,汉安帝(公元106年至125年)在位期间,庆封的后代因其姓氏触犯安帝之父刘庆的名讳,被迫改姓。于是,他们将姓氏由意为“庆祝”的“庆”改为同样含有“庆贺”之意的“贺”。",
