    "en": "Jia",
    "zh": "贾",
    "history": "From the name of the ancient state of Jia, located in present-day Shanxi province. During his reign (1020 BC - 996 BC), King Kang of Zhou granted the state of Jia to his cousin Gongming (公明), who would later be known as Jia Bo (贾伯). The state of Jia was later conquered by the state of Jin during the Spring and Autumn period (771 - 476 BC), and Jia Bo’s descendants adopted Jia as their surname.",
    "historyZh": "源自位于今山西省境内的古贾国之名。周康王在位期间(公元前1020年至前996年),将贾国封给堂弟公明,公明后来被称为贾伯。春秋时期(公元前771年至前476年)贾国被晋国所灭,贾伯的后代便以贾为姓。",
