    "en": "Guo",
    "zh": "郭",
    "history": "From an ancient kingdom located in modern-day Shanxi province. The Guos are believed to be descendants of the Zhou kings. \n\nA younger brother of the famed virtuous Duke Wen Wang (12th cent BC) was granted the kingdom of \"Guo\" and given the name \"Prince Guo Shu\". The original character for Guo kingdom, 虢, means \"to hunt and flay a tiger\", indicating that Prince Guo Shu was a brave warrior. In 658 BC, the state of Guo was annexed by the State of Jin, and descendants of the prince scattered. Eventually, they adopted a different character for their surname Guo.\n\nToday, Guo is a multi-ethnic surname, which has been adopted by Muslim Hui, Mongolian, Manchu, and other ethnic groups throughout the centuries.",
    "historyZh": "源自位于今山西省境内的一个古代王国。郭氏相传是周朝君王的后裔。\n\n著名贤德之君周文王(公元前12世纪)的一位弟弟受封于“虢”国,被称为“虢叔”。虢国之“虢”字本义为“猎杀剥取虎皮”,显示虢叔乃一位骁勇善战的武士。公元前658年,虢国被晋国吞并,王子的后代四散各地。最终,他们将姓氏改用另一个字形“郭”。\n\n如今,郭姓是一个多民族姓氏,历经数百年,已被回族、蒙古族、满族等多个民族所采用。",
