    "en": "Jin",
    "zh": "金",
    "history": "The surname Jin can trace its roots back to Shaohao (少昊), said to be the Yellow Emperor’s son. He was also known by the name Jintian (金天氏). After he died, some of his descendants adopted Jin as their surname. Another known origin of the surname Jin is from Jin Midi (金日䃅), a Xiongnu prince who pledged loyalty to the Han Dynasty. Impressed with his capabilities, Emperor Wu of Han (157-87 BC) granted him the surname Jin, which his descendants still bear till this day.",
