    "en": "Lu",
    "zh": "陆",
    "history": "The surname Lu has two origins, the first of which can trace its roots back to Lu Zhong (陆终), a great-grandson of Emperor Zhuanxu. Lu Zhong was granted the region of Luxiang (陆乡) in present-day Shandong province, and his descendants adopted Lu as their surname. The second origin story states that Duke Xuan of Qi (350-301 BC) granted the same region of Luxiang to his youngest son, Prince Tong (公子通), or Tian Tong (田通). His descendants also came to adopt Lu as their surname.",
    "historyZh": "陆姓有两个起源,第一个可追溯至陆终,颛顼帝的曾孙。陆终受封于位于今山东省境内的陆乡,其后代便以陆为姓。第二个起源说法称,齐宣王(公元前350年至前301年)将同一片陆乡之地封给其幼子公子通(又称田通)。他的后代后来也以陆为姓。",
