    "en": "Gu",
    "zh": "顾",
    "history": "The surname Gu has two origins. The first origin is from the ancient state of Gu, located in present-day Henan province, which was founded during the Xia Dynasty. When it was conquered by King Tang of Shang, its descendants adopted Gu as their surname. The second origin can trace its roots back to Goujian (勾践), King of Yue, who reigned in the late Spring and Autumn period (771-476 BC). During the Han Dynasty (202 BC - 220 AD), a descendant of Goujian was granted the city of Kuaiji in present-day Zhejiang province, and known as Lord Guyu (顾余侯). His descendants would eventually adopt Gu as their surname as well.",
    "historyZh": "顾姓有两个起源。第一个源自位于今河南省境内的古顾国,建于夏朝。该国被商汤所灭后,其后代便以顾为姓。第二个起源可追溯至越王勾践,他在位于春秋末期(公元前771年至前476年)。汉朝(公元前202年至公元220年)时,勾践的一位后裔受封于今浙江省境内的会稽城,被称为“顾余侯”。他的后代最终也以顾为姓。",
